stdout : fun : (a) -> (a, a)
exit : 0

Linear function cannot be discarded
ignore(linfun() { () })
stderr : @.*Type error:.*
exit : 1

Linear function is used once in either branch
var f = linfun(x) { x + 1 }; if (true) {f(41)} else {f(0)}
stdout : 42 : Int

Linear closure can capture a linear function
fun faithfulApply(f:((a::Any) -@ ())) { linfun (s) { f(s) } } faithfulApply
stdout : fun : [] (((a::Any) -@ ()) -> (a::Any) -@ ())

Unrestricted closure cannot capture a linear function
var f = (linfun() { 42 } : [] (() -@ Int)); fun call() { f() } call()
stderr : @.*Type error: Variable f has a linear type.*
exit : 1
